Grape v1.58 Release.

## Summary

  This development cycle delivers major workflow, performance, and GitLab usability improvements since v1.56.1.

### New capabilities

  - Added grape diff, with branch/submodule mapping support, pathspec selection, staged-diff support, Git pager

    integration, and colorized output.

  - Added download support for failing CI job artifacts.

  - Added grape review --printUnresolvedComments to collect unresolved MR discussions across the workspace, with

    commenter filtering.

  - Improved grape push output by surfacing server messages and replacing repetitive MR-creation URLs with a clear

    grape review recommendation.

  - Modernized grape test onto pytest, with parallel execution, targeted changed-test runs, suite sharding, timing

    visibility, and substantially faster full-suite execution.

  - Reworked scoped grape commit infrastructure; commits across submodules and nested subprojects now run in parallel.

### Workspace and subproject reliability

  - Improved checkout, update, merge-down, and new-flow handling for nested-subproject URL changes.

  - Added reliable detection and relocation of renamed/moved submodules, including metadata repair, retry recovery,

    and recursive merge support.

  - Correctly deinitializes and removes submodules removed by a merge, and prevents merge-down crashes caused by stale

    candidates after the public branch removes a submodule.

  - Improved branch selection and missing-branch handling when adding nested subprojects.

  - Clarified force behavior: -F now consistently applies to both submodules and nested subprojects, while checkout

    supports force removal of unclean repositories.

  - Updated --np=-1 to consistently use all available processors.

### Review and GitLab improvements

  - Expanded grape approve input sources and reporting, including datetime/branch inputs and visibility of completed

    repo approvals and existing MR inputs.

  - Improved review behavior for unpushed branches, optional reviewer minimums, approval/tag comparison, and MR-

    description whitespace.

  - Updated GitLab integration for newer permission behavior: GRAPE no longer creates, updates, queries, or deletes

    GitLab approval rules, relying instead on GRAPEs own review checks.

  - Avoided duplicate completed-review verification during publish and improved code-review service/user detection.

### Additional fixes

  - Improved merge-down output, conflict summaries, diagnostics, and error reporting.

  - Added explicit handling for Git index.lock failures.

  - Ensured grape unbundle returns failure when unbundling fails.

  - Fixed remote-tracking branch refresh behavior during grape up.

